 **Warm pools.** A warm sandbox of an `open` environment is on the open network, so it is never claimed for an intake job: the job cold-starts, 30–60 s more. Where that matters, declare a proxied pool: an environment with `egress: {mode: allowlist}` and `warm_pool:` for intake work (map it in `HANGAR_GITHUB_REPOS`), whose warm sandboxes are proxied already. Hosts outside the allowlist go through [egress requests](#egress-allowlists), answered by a person.
 
-**Where it can't run.** The floor needs hangar's egress proxy: `HANGAR_EGRESS_URL` on GKE, hangar on the Linux Docker host itself (not inside Docker Desktop's VM, and not in the Compose container) on Docker. Elsewhere an enforced intake job in an `open` environment fails to start with a message that says so, rather than run unfenced; use `warn` for local work. `hangar doctor` reports the posture, the gateway, the egress proxy per provider, and each environment mapped for intake work with its effective mode. A job queued while the pools are powered down gets the floor when it claims its sandbox.
+**Where it can't run.** The floor needs hangar's egress proxy: `HANGAR_EGRESS_URL` on GKE, hangar on the Linux Docker host itself (not inside Docker Desktop's VM, and not in the Compose container) on Docker. Elsewhere an enforced intake job in an `open` environment fails to start with a message that says so, rather than run unfenced; use `warn` for local work. `hangar doctor` reports the posture, the gateway, the egress proxy per provider, and each environment mapped for intake work with its effective mode. Under `enforce` without the gateway it fails once an intake front door is configured (a GitHub webhook secret, Slack's signing secret, `HANGAR_JIRA`, `HANGAR_GITHUB_PROJECTS` or `HANGAR_INBOUND_WEBHOOKS`), naming the doors whose jobs it refuses; before any is, as on a fresh `hangar up`, nothing is refused and it only warns. Either way its fix is the command that turns the gateway on where hangar runs ([turning it on](#turning-it-on)): on a Linux laptop that is `HANGAR_GATEWAY_URL` and `HANGAR_GATEWAY_HOST` (the gateway binds loopback otherwise, out of the sandboxes' reach) and a restart. A job queued while the pools are powered down gets the floor when it claims its sandbox.
 
